# Local defaults, loaded in every Vite mode.
#
# `npm run dev` is mode development, so it stops here and talks to the partner
# started by `npm run partner` on localhost:5200. A production build loads
# `.env.production` afterwards, which overrides these with the public deployed
# origins. The two origins cannot be derived at runtime: the studio and the
# partner shop are deliberately hosted by different providers, which is the
# whole point of the cross-origin tool exchange. vite.config.ts writes them
# into dist/_headers, and src/mcp/supplier.ts reads VITE_SUPPLIER_ORIGIN to
# find the partner frame.
#
# These are public URLs, not secrets — committed so local dev and
# `npm run build` are reproducible. Without them the build still succeeds, but
# silently ships:
#     Permissions-Policy: tools=(self)
#     Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'
# and the partner iframe is never allowed to publish its tools.

VITE_STUDIO_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5199
VITE_SUPPLIER_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5200
